# Copy to .env.local (gitignored) to build the client against a separate API origin.
#
# Leave unset or empty for the common case: the client and the API are served
# from one origin, the client asks for /api/... relative, and nothing needs
# configuring. `npm run dev` is always this case - Vite proxies /api to :8787.
#
# Set it to an absolute http(s) origin to split them - static hosting for the
# client, a container for the server. It is read at BUILD time and inlined, so
# changing it means rebuilding the client, not restarting anything.
#
# The app must be served over https for the PWA to install, and a https page may
# not call a http API - so in any real deployment this is https too. The client
# refuses to start on that mismatch rather than reporting it as "offline".
#
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.tikerino.example
